# Keeping a qualified description together
#
# Joe is described as a good cobbler using a two-item list. An N3 rule
# preserves that qualified description in a quoted conclusion instead of
# treating good and cobbler as separate facts.
#
# See <https://shs.hal.science/halshs-04148373/document>
# See <http://intrologic.stanford.edu/chapters/chapter_11.html>

@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/ns#> .

# The list keeps good attached to the cobbler qualification.
:joe :is (:good :Cobbler) .

# Match a good-at-a-trade description and return that same description
# inside a graph; no general good-person claim is produced.
{
    ?X :is (:good ?Y) .
} => {
    :test :is {
        ?X :is (:good ?Y)
    } .
} .
